      "writtenOn": "2025-12-02T19:59:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e But then, QI may be stipulated to be only 3 pages (not 4) and QI desc may happen to occupy 5 pages\n\nThat would be addressed (well, detected) by the BUILD_BUG_ON I suggested above, right?\n\nMy actual motivation here is not to prepare for a future scenario with order \u003e 2 (which is unlikely to happen) but just to make it clearer what exactly your code is already doing here (and why its usage of `order` here is correct). What your code is doing is: allocate twice more pages than normally, and allocate `desc_status` at the beginning of the extra pages (i.e. non-overlapping with the original pages). Using `(1 \u003c\u003c (order - 1))` makes it explicit.",
      "parentUuid": "84f69365_78fe8a7b",
